"M","n":"TCPDF::setFontStretching","p":"TCPDF.html#method_setFontStretching","d":null},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::getFontStretching","p":"TCPDF.html#method_getFontStretching","d":""},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::setFontSpacing","p":"TCPDF.html#method_setFontSpacing","d":null},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::getFontSpacing","p":"TCPDF.html#method_getFontSpacing","d":""},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::getPageRegions","p":"TCPDF.html#method_getPageRegions","d":null},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::setPageRegions","p":"TCPDF.html#method_setPageRegions","d":null},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::addPageRegion","p":"TCPDF.html#method_addPageRegion","d":null},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::removePageRegion","p":"TCPDF.html#method_removePageRegion","d":null},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::currentPageNoWriteAreas","p":"TCPDF.html#method_currentPageNoWriteAreas","d":"<p>The legacy no-write areas registered for the current page, in the engine\nsetNoWriteRegions() input format (xt/yt/xb/yb/side).</p>"},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::applyNoWriteRegionsForFlow","p":"TCPDF.html#method_applyNoWriteRegionsForFlow","d":"<p>(Re)build the engine banded writable regions for the current page from\nits legacy no-write areas, using $bandheight as the height of each\nhorizontal slice, then select the region that contains the current Y so\nthe flow starts at the cursor and hugs the obstacles band by band. The\ntext/HTML engine then advances region -&gt; region -&gt; fresh full-width page\non its own.</p>"},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::selectRegionAtY","p":"TCPDF.html#method_selectRegionAtY","d":"<p>Select the (top-to-bottom ordered) writable region of the current page\nwhose vertical span contains $y, so a flow that starts at the cursor\nbegins in the right band. Falls back to the first region when $y sits\nabove them all.</p>"},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::noWriteBandFromHtml","p":"TCPDF.html#method_noWriteBandFromHtml","d":"<p>Band height (one writable slice) for a no-write region flow of HTML: the\ncell height of the body (outermost) font size declared in the fragment,\nfalling back to the current font. A slice should be about one body line\ntall so the bands hug the obstacle without wasting vertical space (which\nwould push too much text onto the continuation page); larger inline runs\nsit in the tall merged region at the top rather than at a band boundary.</p>"},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF::ImageSVG","p":"TCPDF.html#method_ImageSVG","d":null},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF_ENGINE::setPageContext","p":"TCPDF_ENGINE.html#method_setPageContext","d":null},{"t":"M","n":"TCPDF_ENGINE::anchorPageRegionsToContentTop","p":"TCPDF_ENGINE.html#method_anchorPageRegionsToContentTop","d":"<p>Anchor the page regions (columns) at the content top margin.</p>"},{"t":"N","n":"","p":"[Global_Namespace].html"}]}
